<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mühlberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1547</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-war">Schmalkaldic War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mühlberg was fought on 24 April 1547 near Mühlberg on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a> and decided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schmalkaldic-war">Schmalkaldic War</a>. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-alvarez-de-toledo-3rd-duke-of-alba">Duke of Alba</a> crossed the river, surprised the Protestant army of Elector John Frederick I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> and captured the elector. By the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capitulation-of-wittenberg">Capitulation of Wittenberg</a> that followed, the electoral title passed to Maurice of Saxony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albertine-line">Albertine line</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-muhlberg.jpg" alt="Battle of Mühlberg" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LUIS DE AVILA Y ZUNIGA (c.1490 C. 1560) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schlacht_bei_M%C3%BChlberg_1547.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
